  "summary": "The study fabricated three Ti3C2Tx negative-electrode films: pristine Ti3C2Tx, Mn2+-exchanged Ti3C2Tx-Mn, and annealed Mn2+-exchanged a-Ti3C2Tx-Mn; it also fabricated a RuO2/SWCNT positive reference electrode for an asymmetric device. Ti3C2Tx was prepared by mild LiF/HCl etching, while the modified films additionally underwent KOH pretreatment and Mn2+ exchange; the headline film was annealed at 400 \u00b0C under Ar for 2 h. The primary a-Ti3C2Tx-Mn electrode delivered the best reported GCD capacitance, 401 F g-1 at 1 A g-1 in 1 M H2SO4. Film thickness, unambiguous mass loading, BET surface area, porosity, pore size, and volumetric/areal capacitance were not reported."
